Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: describe MSM8996 split CTLs and fbdev RAM mapping

MSM8996 supports split display on CTL0/1, as also reserved by mdp5_ctlm_init.
Without these capabilities DPU rejects the dual-DSI panel with ENAVAIL.
Mark both controls so the existing DPU split-display path can allocate them.

The msm fbdev implementation uses a GEM vmap and sysmem fb helpers; mark it
FBINFO_VIRTFB consistently with drm_fbdev_shmem to avoid sysmem helper warnings.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_1_7_msm8996.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_1_7_msm8996.h
@@ -43,9 +43,11 @@
 	{
 		.name = "ctl_0", .id = CTL_0,
 		.base = 0x1000, .len = 0x64,
+		.features = BIT(DPU_CTL_SPLIT_DISPLAY),
 	}, {
 		.name = "ctl_1", .id = CTL_1,
 		.base = 0x1200, .len = 0x64,
+		.features = BIT(DPU_CTL_SPLIT_DISPLAY),
 	}, {
 		.name = "ctl_2", .id = CTL_2,
 		.base = 0x1400, .len = 0x64,
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
@@ -134,6 +134,7 @@
 	fbi->fbops = &msm_fb_ops;
 
 	drm_fb_helper_fill_info(fbi, helper, sizes);
+	fbi->flags |= FBINFO_VIRTFB; /* GEM buffer mapped into system memory */
 
 	fbi->screen_buffer = msm_gem_get_vaddr(bo);
 	if (IS_ERR(fbi->screen_buffer)) {
